    "text": "Is there a constant δ with 0 < δ < 1 and an integer N such that whenever\nA, B, and C are conjugacy classes in the alternating group Alt(n) each of size at least\n|Alt(n)|δ with n ⩾ N , then ABC = Alt(n)?                      M. Garonzi, A. Maróti\n  ∗ Yes, there are (D. Dona, Preprint, 2025, https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.06012).\n\n                                √",
